From f61977a8cc02c5f34aa0b280ceee1306bf043750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:46:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/adbe: Verify translated display scanout before enabling
 planes

Fullscreen client buffers cannot scan out directly while the display
fetches physically contiguous memory in bypass, adding a compositor pass.
Map scanout buffers through the display DART so imported dma-bufs form a
single device-address range. Preserve the boot framebuffer mapping before
deferred attachment and hold each displayed buffer through its last fetch.

Require a live pipe-CRC self-check before using translated planes. Scan out
an owned asymmetric pattern in bypass, through a nonidentity mapping, and
through an alias with two 16 KiB pages swapped. Enable blend CRC directly at
ADP +0x1074, restore its previous value, and require stable nonzero reference
CRCs, matching translated CRCs, a different permuted CRC and no DART/SMMU
faults. Report per-step pipe errors; output underrun alone is diagnostic.

Always restore the previous framebuffer after the check. On failure or an
inconclusive result, restore bypass and verify both translation controls.
Retain live mappings if the previous framebuffer or rollback cannot be
confirmed. Shutdown parks on the boot framebuffer before disabling both
front ends. There is no option to bypass verification; the existing
read-only dart_scanout parameter remains a boot-time disable switch.

Only a display pipe with a scanout DMA child takes the new path. Both SoCs
use the same mapping-before-attach and mandatory CRC check. If the CRC enable
does not read back, restore its control without flipping or attaching. A
zero or unstable reference, or an ineffective page permutation, also returns
to bypass. Restore the prior image before returning from any displayed test.

Affects: Apple A9 and A10 display scanout.

Assisted-by: LLM
